md runs the two lines together with no space at all, printing
"First line of the notesecond line of the note." as one word pair.

MarkdownParser.getNodeText renders every non-text inline node with
cmark_render_commonmark and then trims it. A soft break renders as a
single newline, which the trim reduces to the empty string, so the
line break between the two lines disappears and the words on either
side of it are joined. A soft wrap must survive, or at the very least
leave the space that held the two words apart.
